  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Ht-2 Toxin and Phosphodiesterase 6C, as multiple compounds identified as targets of Ht-2 Toxin are also targets of Phosphodiesterase 6C. Specifically, LoVo, a cell line that is a target of Ht-2 Toxin, is also a target of two distinct compounds—Kadlongilactone A and 1-(3-Oxo-undecyldisulfanyl)-undecan-3-one—both of which have a direct interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that Ht-2 Toxin may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the activation or modulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, potentially by influencing the cellular environment or signaling pathways that regulate this enzyme. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, reinforcing the hypothesis that Ht-2 Toxin may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a shared biological process, such as cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
